From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:27:50 -0400
Subject: feat: Settings in cards, the drift mark as a setting, one question
 for a session

Settings > Stedding was one long card with the groups under headings. It is
now a card per group, named as the setup screen names its steps: Sidebar,
Tabs, Peek and little windows (a card of its own, out of Pages), Spaces,
Sync and import (the sidebar file, sync through a folder and the Arc
import, out of Spaces), Pages and menus, Privacy, Updates and Shortcuts.
The first card carries the page's line and the groups' names, each a
button that scrolls its card into view. Every row has room above and below
its text, each row's line says what it does in one short sentence (most ran
two to four lines), the sidebar file's buttons sit under its text, Spaces
are parted by lines and each names its session switch (settings T13).
Every string on the page was read again: one apostrophe, "address row"
throughout, sentence-case buttons, "such as" in every field, plain names for
the hover delay and Chromium's ad features, and command names in the
Shortcuts list without asides. The Shortcuts list's remove buttons drew a
plain grey disc beside every key: the editor loads no shared icon styles, so
it names the icon itself, and each key and its button share one outline.

"Mark pinned tabs that left their page" (stedding.pins.mark_drifted, off
by default) decides whether a pinned tab away from its home shows the dot
on its essentials card and in the collapsed rail, and the reset control on
the card under the pointer. Off, neither shows; a Space-pinned row keeps
its slash, and Reset to Pinned Page stays on the tab's menu. It is in the
Tabs card and the command bar, and reaches every row at once (pins H28,
GitHub issue 36).

A Space's session switch in Settings asks the question the Space menu and
the command bar ask, SetSpaceIsolatedAfterAsking: it had a dialog of its
own about open pages alone, so with only apps made in the Space it turned
the session off at once and never named them (sessions S10).

Why: the owner, 2026-10-26 (Settings grouped like the setup screen, S-313,
and on beta 19's page: "Super overcrowded", "make sure it's perfect
everywhere";
issue 36's setting, off by default, S-305; review finding S-318).
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
